KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp23
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ at run time: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static_assert condition could not be evaluated
--
The parser kept only the run-time branch of `if consteval' (and of `if
!consteval'), so constant evaluation took it too: the static assertions
failed.  Both branches are now kept, under __builtin_is_constant_evaluated()
([meta.const.eval]/1), which constant evaluation folds to true.
